<h2 class="bold" id="recommendations"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="text-input#recommendations">Recommendations</a></h2>
<ul>
<li>Match virtual keyboard with expected data.<!-- -->
<ul>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">type=&quot;email&quot;</span></span></code></span> when asking for an email address puts the @ sign directly on the main keyboard.</li>
<li><span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">pattern=&quot;[0-9]*&quot; inputmode=&quot;numeric&quot;</span></span></code></span> attributes opens numeric keyboard. avoid using <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">type=&quot;number&quot;</span></span></code></span> when the requested information is not a pure number that can be incremented (e.g. phone number, ZIP code, etc.). <a href="https://technology.blog.gov.uk/2020/02/24/why-the-gov-uk-design-system-team-changed-the-input-type-for-numbers/" class="underline">Why not to use input type=&quot;number&quot;</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
